{"title":"2010 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_by_MathTalks\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video by MathTalks</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The two circles pictured have the same center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Chord <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbb4c52e011ceed6e813118a7d59e931af444a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> is tangent to the inner circle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and chord <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbb4c52e011ceed6e813118a7d59e931af444a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. What is the area between the two circles?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/f/2cfa82378d1bafff2108201dd94835ed7a9aab8d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(45); import graph; size(300); real lsf = 0.5; pen dp = linewidth(0.7) + fontsize(10); defaultpen(dp); pen ds = black; pen xdxdff = rgb(0.49,0.49,1); draw((2,0.15)--(1.85,0.15)--(1.85,0)--(2,0)--cycle); draw(circle((2,1),2.24)); draw(circle((2,1),1)); draw((0,0)--(4,0)); draw((0,0)--(2,1)); draw((2,1)--(2,0)); draw((2,1)--(4,0)); dot((0,0),ds); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, (-0.19,-0.23),NE*lsf); dot((2,0),ds); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, (1.97,-0.31),NE*lsf); dot((2,1),ds); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, (1.96,1.09),NE*lsf); dot((4,0),ds); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, (4.07,-0.24),NE*lsf); clip((-3.1,-7.72)--(-3.1,4.77)--(11.74,4.77)--(11.74,-7.72)--cycle); [/asy]\" width=\"345\" height=\"338\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/c/34c9b53624466c0ccdeb42ee4daaaa478f49d9cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 36 \\pi \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 49 \\pi\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 64 \\pi\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 81 \\pi\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 100 \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"458\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f7a55113a84ee4c04eb66f66d08310c32533ca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is isosceles, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3a4ec0df571e719bd3f1d7e00bf71fc55ba2b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> bisects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/1/3417076b3ee8dd300b4464e2d0e71a5e5e0323bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=BD=8$\" width=\"115\" height=\"13\" />. From the Pythagorean Theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/1/7917c1676432c5fd214899a833c5b6d66b993558.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB=6$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" />. Thus the area between the two circles is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/5/145911f211249d0d620081bdeb67a975eb8fbb77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100\\pi - 36\\pi=64\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"142\" height=\"13\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/a/69a823935261d8ff641cdcd8ec643f31b9b38e1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 64\\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"75\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>Note: The length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is necessary information, as this tells us the radius of the larger circle.  The area of the annulus is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/5/7b59b1a839e2422ea7c93c7c1617ece314e07d37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi(AC^2-BC^2)=\\pi AB^2=64\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"243\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Q6rnoQChiyU\">https://youtu.be/Q6rnoQChiyU</a>. Soo, DRMS, NM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/51K3uCzntWs?t=3206\">https://youtu.be/51K3uCzntWs?t=3206</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_by_MathTalks\">Video by MathTalks</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video by MathTalks\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KSYVsSJDX-0&amp;feature=youtu.be\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KSYVsSJDX-0&amp;feature=youtu.be</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/yjhitUYSAI0\">https://youtu.be/yjhitUYSAI0</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8\" title=\"2010 AMC 8\">2010 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2010 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2010 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2010\">Resou